			
	
		
                              CyberCNET v 1.1
                              ---------------

    CyberCNET is a tool for exhausted SysOp's that doesn't havet the time 
    to check how motivated all the new users are or if it's hard for a new
    user show how motivated he/she are. For example, if you got a lot of 
    old users that written a lot of messages, uploaded many files and so 
    on, SysOp will have trouble to see that the new users actually are a
    good user and deserves higher access. Then you, as a SysOp, shuold be 
    using CyberCNET!!


                      What's new in CyberCNET v1.1 ??
                      -------------------------------

    Well, the only thing fixed is the little bug, which gave the user only
    one step higher acc, even if the next level defined was 3 steps higher,
    i.e if you'd defined level 1 ,and the next level you'ved defined was
    no 5, the person using tho old CyberCNET whould get status 2. And that 
    wasn't very funny, but it's now fixed.



                         What does CyberCNET do ??
                         -------------------------

    Well, When a new user had uploaded a lot's of files (and many kB's )
    and written awully much public messages and been calling a lot he/she
    run's the CyberCNET and it'll check if he/she's been active enough 
    and if so higher there access. SysOp doesn't have to do a thing,except
    to config the program correctly, about access, just leave the work to
    CyberCNET and let the right users get the right access!!


                    
                         How to install CyberCNET.
                         -------------------------

    Nothing could be easier than to install CyberCNET! Copy the Arexx
    file called Cyber.rexx to anywhere in you're PFILES: directory.
    Copy Levels.cfg to the SYSDATA: directory. Then ju just have to 
    add it to your Pfiles-list. No special adjustment is needed.



                         How to config CyberCNET.
                         ------------------------

    In the mainfile Cyber.rexx all you should change is the MaxLevels				
    you wan't a user to beable to reach. MaxLevels 10 is current.
    the second thing in the Cyber.rexx-file to alter is bbsname, if
    you don't wan't my board name of course.

    In the levels.cfg file all you have to do is to be shure that you've
    got enough levels defined according to the MaxLevels in the main 
    file. The syntax for the .cfg file is as follows :

    1	   /* Level to attend */
    80    /* kB's uploaded by User*/
    5    /* Number of files uploaded */	
    10  /* Numberof public messages written */	
    5  /* Number of calls made */

    5 /* The next level to attend, i.e skipping 3 steps.... */

    When the user done all the things defined in our config-file,
    CyberCNET will give the user next accesslevel as soon as he run's
    the util.	
    
    !! Be sure to have a CR after each leveldefination is completed. !!


                      Who's allowed to use CyberCNET?
                      -------------------------------

     Well, anyone can use the program as they want's as long as they obey 
     the following rules :

      1./  You must be REGISTRATED user of C-Net.

      2./  You may not alter ANYTHING in the files except for what is 
           stated above.

      3./  If you gonna spread the tools , you MUST have all the files 
           in it's original archive

     If you follow these rules, everything is OK!



